{
  "id": "18-procurement-guideline",
  "title": "Procurement Guideline",
  "approxPages": 3,
  "wordCount": 1622,
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Procurement Guideline"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Guideline no. GL-PUR-01, version 4.0. Owner: [PERSON_1], Head of Purchasing, [ORG_1]. Approved by the management board on [DATE_1] and valid for all sites from [DATE_2]."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. Purpose and Scope"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This guideline sets out how [ORG_1] buys goods and services. It is intended to make sure that we buy at the right quality, at competitive prices and on time, that purchasing decisions are transparent and traceable, and that all employees involved act in line with the law and our code of conduct."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The guideline applies to all purchases of production material, indirect material, services, investments and software by [ORG_1] and its subsidiaries in Germany, regardless of the cost centre or the budget from which they are paid. It applies to all employees who request, negotiate, order or approve purchases. Purchases between companies of the group and the hiring of employees are not covered by this guideline."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Over the past two years, the number of suppliers we work with has grown from about 1,400 to more than 2,100, mainly because of small orders placed directly by departments. At the same time, the share of spend that was negotiated by the purchasing department fell to 71 percent. This version of the guideline therefore puts more emphasis on bundling demand, using framework agreements and choosing suppliers from the approved supplier list."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. Principles"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "All purchasing activities follow these principles:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Separation of duties:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " the person who requests a purchase does not approve it alone, and the person who orders does not confirm the receipt of the goods."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Competition:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " we obtain several offers wherever this is reasonable and choose the supplier with the best overall value, not simply the lowest price."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Transparency:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " every purchasing decision is documented in the ERP system so that a third party can understand it later."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Fairness:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " all suppliers receive the same information at the same time and are treated equally in a tender."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Integrity:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " employees do not accept gifts or invitations that could influence their decisions, in line with the anti-corruption policy."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Sustainability:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " we consider environmental and social criteria when we select a supplier, as described in section 7."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3. Roles and Responsibilities"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ],
            "text": "Requesting departments"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " identify their demand, describe it clearly in a purchase requisition and make sure that budget is available. For technical goods and services, they prepare the specification and take part in the technical evaluation of offers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ],
            "text": "The purchasing department"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is responsible for the selection of suppliers, the request for quotations, negotiations and the conclusion of contracts and framework agreements. Only employees of the purchasing department are authorised to commit [ORG_1] to a supplier, with the exceptions listed in section 4.4. The purchasing department also maintains the approved supplier list and carries out the annual supplier evaluation."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ],
            "text": "Approvers"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " check whether a purchase is necessary and covered by the budget, and approve it in the ERP system according to the approval limits in section 5. Approvers are named in the signature regulations of [ORG_1]."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ],
            "text": "Quality management"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " approves new suppliers of production material, carries out supplier audits and handles complaints about defective deliveries together with the purchasing department."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ],
            "text": "Accounts payable"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " pays invoices only if they match an approved purchase order and a confirmed receipt of goods or services."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4. Procurement Process"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4.1 Purchase Requisition"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every purchase starts with a purchase requisition in the ERP system. The requisition must contain a clear description of the goods or services, the quantity, the required delivery date, the cost centre and, where known, a suggested supplier. For technical goods, the requesting department attaches the specification. Requisitions for software and IT services must also be reviewed by the IT department before they are sent to purchasing, to check compatibility, licensing and information security."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4.2 Request for Quotation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The purchasing department obtains offers depending on the expected order value:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Up to EUR 5,000 net: one offer is sufficient if the price is plausible, for example based on previous orders or a price list."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "From EUR 5,000 to EUR 50,000 net: at least three written offers."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Above EUR 50,000 net: a structured tender with at least three suppliers."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "orderedList",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "The specification and the evaluation criteria are defined before the tender starts."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "All suppliers receive the same tender documents through the supplier portal."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Offers are opened together by two employees of purchasing after the deadline."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "listItem",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Questions from suppliers and the answers are shared with all participants."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If fewer offers than required can be obtained, for example because only one supplier can deliver a certain spare part, the reason is documented in the purchase file."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4.3 Award and Contract"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The purchasing department evaluates the offers together with the requesting department, based on price, quality, delivery time, total cost of ownership and the supplier evaluation. The result and the reasons for the decision are documented in the purchase file. For orders above EUR 50,000 net, the award decision is signed by the head of purchasing and the head of the requesting department."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "For recurring demand, purchasing concludes framework agreements with fixed prices and conditions for usually one to three years. Departments then order from the framework agreement through the ERP system without a new request for quotation. Contracts with a value above EUR 250,000 or with unusual liability provisions are reviewed by the legal department before signature."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4.4 Ordering"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Purchase orders are created in the ERP system and sent to the supplier by the purchasing department. Our general "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "https://example.com/purchasing/terms-and-conditions"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "terms and conditions of purchase"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " are part of every order. Orders placed orally or by email without a purchase order are not permitted, except in the following cases:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Orders from framework agreements through the catalogues in the ERP system"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Small purchases up to EUR 250 net with a company purchasing card, in line with the purchasing card policy"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Emergency orders to avoid a production stop or damage, which must be followed by a purchase order within two working days"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "5. Approval Limits"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Purchase requisitions are approved in the ERP system according to the following limits. The limits refer to the total net order value, including all planned call-offs of the order. Splitting an order to stay below an approval limit is not permitted."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Net order value"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Approval by"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Number of offers"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Additional requirements"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "up to EUR 5,000"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "head of cost centre"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "1"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "none"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "EUR 5,000 to EUR 25,000"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "head of department"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "3"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "comparison of offers in the purchase file"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "EUR 25,000 to EUR 50,000"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "head of division"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "3"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "comparison of offers in the purchase file"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "EUR 50,000 to EUR 250,000"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "managing director"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "tender"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "award decision signed by purchasing"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "above EUR 250,000"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "management board"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "tender"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableCell",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "review by legal department"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Investments must also be approved in the annual investment plan. If an investment exceeds the approved amount by more than 10 percent, a new approval is required."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "6. Supplier Selection and Evaluation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "6.1 Approved Supplier List"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The purchasing department maintains a list of approved suppliers in the ERP system. New suppliers are added to the list after a check of their financial stability, their certificates and, for production material, a quality audit or a sample inspection. Orders should be placed with suppliers on the approved supplier list whenever possible. If a department wants to work with a new supplier, it informs the purchasing department early, because the approval of a new supplier of production material usually takes six to eight weeks."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "6.2 Annual Supplier Evaluation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every year in January, the purchasing department evaluates all suppliers with an annual purchasing volume of more than EUR 50,000 and all suppliers of production material. The evaluation uses the following criteria and weights:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "tableRow",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Criterion"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Weight"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "tableHeader",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Basis of assessment"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
