      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Suppliers are classified as A (preferred supplier, at least 85 points), B (approved supplier, 70 to 84 points) or C (supplier with need for improvement, below 70 points). With C suppliers, the purchasing department agrees an improvement plan with clear targets and deadlines. If the targets are not met within twelve months, no new orders are placed with the supplier unless there is no alternative."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "7. Sustainability and Compliance"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "[ORG_1] expects all suppliers to comply with the law and with the principles of our "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "https://example.com/purchasing/supplier-code-of-conduct"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "supplier code of conduct"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The code of conduct covers human rights, working conditions, environmental protection, anti-corruption and fair competition. It is part of every framework agreement and is accepted by every new supplier during registration."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "As a company with more than 1,000 employees in Germany, [ORG_1] is subject to the Supply Chain Due Diligence Act. The purchasing department therefore carries out an annual risk analysis of our direct suppliers, based on their country, their industry and the results of the sustainability questionnaire. Suppliers with an increased risk are asked for additional information or audited. If we learn of a violation, we work with the supplier on corrective measures, and as a last resort we end the business relationship."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Employees who learn of a possible violation by a supplier, or of a breach of this guideline, can report it to the compliance officer, [PERSON_2], at [EMAIL_1], or anonymously through the whistleblower system."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "8. Exceptions"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Exceptions to this guideline require the written approval of the head of purchasing and, for order values above EUR 50,000, of the managing director. The reason for the exception is documented in the purchase file. The purchasing department reports all exceptions to the management board once a quarter."
          }
        ]
      },
